  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Romans",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 12,
    "summary": "Paul counsels the Saints to present their bodies as a living sacrifice, to use their own grace-given gifts, and to live as Saints should live.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Body, Sanctity of."
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "Mosiah 2:34; Moro. 10:32 (30–33); D&C 93:1. TG Self-Sacrifice."
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "Lev. 1:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "TG Service."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 141
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG World; Worldliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Eph. 5:8; 1 Jn. 5:4 (1–5). TG Self-Mastery."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Man, New, Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Mind."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "GR test, try, prove."
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 158,
            "text": "TG God, Will of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For I say, through the grace given unto me, to every man that is among you, not to think of himself more highly than he ought to think; but to think soberly, according as God hath dealt to every man the measure of faith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          },
          {
            "start": 149,
            "end": 156,
            "text": "D&C 18:21; 43:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 171,
            "end": 174,
            "text": "1 Cor. 7:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For as we have many members in one body, and all members have not the same office:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "GR function, operation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So we, being many, are one body in Christ, and every one members one of another.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Unity."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, let us prophesy according to the proportion of faith;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 142,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 105
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Or ministry, let us wait on our ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth, let him do it with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 157,
            "text": "TG Cheerful."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let love be without dissimulation. Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "GR sincere, unfeigned, real."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Ps. 26:4; 2 Ne. 4:31; Alma 13:12; D&C 38:42. TG Evil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honour preferring one another;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Philip. 2:2 (1–4)."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "GR haste, diligence."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Zeal."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "D&C 24:8; 31:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Adversity."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "GR constantly persisting in."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Distributing to the necessity of saints; given to hospitality.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "TG Hospitality."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Bless them which persecute you: bless, and curse not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Enemies; Persecution."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Compassion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be of the same mind one toward another. Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate. Be not wise in your own conceits.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "GR conforming willingly with the humble. 3 Ne. 12:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "Prov. 26:12. TG Pride."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Recompense to no man evil for evil. Provide things honest in the sight of all men.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Forgive; Retribution."
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Evil."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "2 Cor. 8:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Prov. 3:30. TG Peace; Peacemakers."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Forbear; Retribution."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 6:22. TG Enemies."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Rev. 2:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
